Changes from 3.0.3 to 3.0.4
===========================

*Updated:
- The search field of the admin page frame has a visually hidden label (the admin design's .a4-sr-only
  class), in the enabled and the disabled state, and the close link of the search scope has a name. The
  Section list of the search scope is bound to its label.
- The search field of the admin search page has a visually hidden label, as in the kernel's template.
- The search fields of the standard, ezwebin and ezdemo search pages, of the ezwebin page header and of
  the ezflow search block are named for screen readers (aria-label), and the ezdemo product's quantity
  field too.
- The labels of the standard design's advanced search are bound to their fields.
- The edit and trash icons of the standard design's Elevate list have alternative text, and the search
  query and language of a new elevation are named for screen readers.

No new strings: the labels reuse existing translations.
